{"term":"salad","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:94b984629344a9a7ea","definition":"A food consisting principally of raw vegetables (especially greens, e.g. lettuce), other savoury ingredients (typically cooked), fruit, or confectionary; often involving two or more such ingredients mixed together, with larger items cut or torn into small pieces, and usually with a dressing or binding; usually served cold or at room temperature, as a dish or savoury sandwich filling.","example":"Lafeu. ’Twas a good lady, ’twas a good lady: we may pick a thousand salads ere we light on such another herb.\nClown. Indeed, sir, she was the sweet marjoram of the salad, or rather, the herb of grace.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["angry fruit salad","cabbage salad","Cæsar salad","chef's salad","chicken salad air","combination salad","composed salad","dinner salad","fiesta salad","gelatine salad","gelatin salad","green salad","ham salad","jello salad","jewel salad","macaroni salad","mac salad","malfouf salad","Moscow salad","perfection salad","poké salad","salad bar","salad bird","salad bowl","salad burnet","salad cream","salad days","salad dodger","salad-dodger","salad dressing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salad#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:622b48a30305bcbcdd","definition":"One or more raw vegetables of the kind used in salads; typically greens (especially lettuce).","example":"sandwiches comprising a meat, a cheese, a salad, and a condiment","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["angry fruit salad","cabbage salad","Cæsar salad","chef's salad","chicken salad air","combination salad","composed salad","dinner salad","fiesta salad","gelatine salad","gelatin salad","green salad","ham salad","jello salad","j